DTSTAMP:20260924T124549Z
SUMMARY:Celebrating 10 Years of The Hmm + Book Launch
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
DTSTART:20261211T180000Z
DTEND:20261211T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:Earlier this year\, the internet was briefly filled with the ho
 pe that 2026 might become the new 2016. In quasi-historical fashion\, user
 s resurfaced early Instagram filters and interfaces\, Tumblr-motivational 
 quotes\, old memes\, and other fragments of a supposedly simpler internet.
  Collectively\, it became a meditation on how social media used to be bett
 er\, or at least how much it felt better. Though users relied on a more ge
 neralised nostalgia to resurrect the aesthetic of the time\, they were\, i
 n a sense\, correct. The internet really did feel different. 2016 was the 
 year that all news feeds became algorithmic\, and with it our relationship
  with social media fundamentally changed.\n‎\n\nSerendipitously\, The Hm
 m was also born ten years ago\, in 2016. Since then\, we have tried to tra
 ce\, interrogate and intervene in the forces shaping our online lives\, in
 cluding the algorithmic feed itself. To celebrate this legacy\, we are thr
 owing a festive evening at W139 in Amsterdam\, filled with performances\, 
 workshops\, drinks and more.\n‎\n‎Suggested For You: Reflecting on a d
 ecade in the feed\nThe evening will also mark the launch of our 10-year an
 niversary publication: Suggested For You: Reflecting on a Decade in the Fe
 ed. Part celebration\, part reflection\, the book looks back at the algori
 thmic feed and the decade of internet cultures that has unfolded around it
 . Featuring essays\, interviews\, image contributions and artist profiles 
 from Ruba Al-Sweel\, Evelyn Austin and Rejo Zenger\, Jak Ritger\, Soyun Pa
 rk and Leo Scarin\, Noura Tafeche\, Neema Githere\, Alex Quicho\, Constant
  Dullaart\, Mamali Shafahi and Ali Eslami\, Danielle Brathwaite-Shirley\, 
 K Allado McDowell and Aidan Walker\, the publication brings together a ran
 ge of perspectives on how the algorithmic feed has come to shape life onli
 ne.\nYou can already pre-order the book. It will be available to pick-up a
 nd purchase at the event.\n‎\nProgram\nSpeakers\, workshops and performa
 nces to be announced soon.\n‎\nWhat you need to know\n\n📅 Date: Frida
 y 11 December 2026\n🕗 Times: 19.00 – 22.00 CET\n📍 Location: W139\,
  Warmoesstraat 139\, 1012 JB Amsterdam\n🎟 Tickets: Free\, but please re
 gister!\n‎\n\n‎💚 This programme is kindly supported by the Amsterda
 ms Fonds voor de Kunsten and Het Cultuurfonds. Suggested For You is suppor
 ted by Mondriaanfonds.
URL:https://thehmm.nl/event/celebrating-10-years-of-the-hmm-book-launch/
CATEGORIES:The Hmm
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:784b736186fce05be5e60324a2ec978823e672ca45dbe5175dfe9c2895156008@pruts-
 agenda.local
